WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.570
A Sikh poem says everything
comes to be by God's command.

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.640
No one is outside it.

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.820
Sikhs call this hukam.

4
00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:12.820
Yet Sikhs meditate, serve
others and work honestly,

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.850
every day, as if their effort matters.

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.400
The same poem says the way to
God is to walk in God's will.

7
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:26.710
So if everything happens by God's will, does
a Sikh's own effort make any difference?

8
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.060
In this mission, you'll
unpack three linked ideas:

9
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:34.420
the Name, God's will, and
what Sikhs call nadar.

10
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.450
Then you'll test these
ideas on a real case:

11
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.260
a Sikh whose business has just failed.

12
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.270
Your mission: find out whether, for Sikhs,

13
00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.990
effort makes any difference
in a world run by God's will.
